WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Two women shape large clay vessels by hand in a workshop in Sejnane, northern Tunisia.

00:12.000 --> 00:30.000
A potter smooths the wet clay and explains in French how she came to love this work.

00:30.000 --> 00:48.000
Close views show mineral pigments and simple tools used to decorate the pottery.

00:48.000 --> 01:08.000
Finished vessels are fired outdoors beneath ash and organic fuel.

01:08.000 --> 01:32.800
A Sejnane potter presents the distinctive forms and motifs of a practice transmitted through generations. French speech is captioned in the video; this English track describes the visuals.
